### CoreVault — M2M Authentication
### Obtain a Bearer token using client credentials.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@clientId = your-client-id
@clientSecret = your-client-secret

# ─── Step 1: Exchange credentials for token ───────────────────────────────────
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "client_id": "{{clientId}}",
  "client_secret": "{{clientSecret}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK
### {
###   "access_token": "eyJ...",
###   "token_type": "Bearer",
###   "expires_in": 3600
### }

# ─── Step 2: Who am I? ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name me
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}

### Expected: 200 OK — returns tenant/user identity
